      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Originalism is the only valid method for interpreting the Constitution because it respects the democratic will of the Founding Fathers and prevents unelected judges from rewriting the law based on their own personal preferences. Living constitutionalism is fundamentally flawed because it allows the judiciary to act as a super-legislature, substituting their own moral views for the text and history that the people explicitly agreed upon. The Second Amendment clearly protects an individual's right to keep and bear arms for self-defense, a right that was understood by the Framers as essential to liberty and has been consistently upheld by the Supreme Court since *Heller*.",
