      "content": "I see. So, if we follow the logic that originalism is the only way to prevent judges from acting like a \"super-legislature,\" does that mean any constitutional amendment process that isn't strictly tied to the historical intent of the Framers essentially undermines the legitimacy of the American legal system?",
